ta:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T14:33:21-07:00","id":188930,"title":"","content":"How about local?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://syvnews.com/news/local/polo-posy-returning-to-court-over--acre-chumash-reservation/article_7d0422e4-b707-5785-8ebd-ff5389ced76a.html\" target=\"_blank\">POLO, POSY returning to court over 6.9-acre Chumash reservation expansion</a><br /> <br /> So recently, the Santa Ynez band of Chumash managed to win a court battle that has been going on for years over a piece of land in Santa Barbara. It looks like they will be going back to court again because some people of Santa Barbara think this section of land will be expansion for the Chumash Casino. While the Casino itself is going to see expansion, this section of land won (<i>Camp 4</i>) isn't part of that plan at all.<br /> <br /> I happen to be of Chumash descent, and I feel that the people of Santa Barbara opposing this do not seem to be aware of irony of the highest magnitude (<i>Being afraid that the Chumash will develop on land that originally belonged to them</i>).<br /> <br /> Then again, we still have people in California that complain about illegal immigrants and seem to be not aware that California was originally part of Mexico and way before that, Spain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:33:34-07:00","id":189029,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not that we\u2019re not aware of that fact as it is that we don\u2019t consider it to be particularly relevant to the current situation. \u201cCalifornia was once part of Mexico, and therefore Mexicans should be free to come and go as they please and do whatever they like regardless of the current government\u201d does not make sense to me. Add to that the fact that the current influx of illegal immigrants are primarily <i>not</i> Mexican, and the matter of prior ownership by Mexico becomes even more irrelevant: you have to fall back on \u201c\u2026and before that, Spain\u201d to maintain even the shreds of validity that the argument had. <br /> <br /> Frankly, this tendency to assume that people who disagree with you are stupid or ignorant (or malicious) is a big part of why the current political climate in the United States is so polarized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:56:00-07:00","id":189042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189029#post189029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, this tendency to assume that people who disagree with you are stupid or ignorant (or malicious) is a big part of why the current political climate in the United States is so polarized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that I am not pointing at Laughing Hyena when I say that: I agree with this sentiment whole-heatedly in the general sense (not towards any user here, in particular, necessarily).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:57:36-07:00","id":189045,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.c-span.org/video/?320264-1/government-surveillance-privacy\" target=\"_blank\">Here is an interesting panel on Section 701 Surveillance.</a><br /> <br /> Section 701 is the surveillance that was partially exposed by Snowden (among other things). See the board's recommendations for policy for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T20:44:55-07:00","id":189144,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189029#post189029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not that we\u2019re not aware of that fact as it is that we don\u2019t consider it to be particularly relevant to the current situation. \u201cCalifornia was once part of Mexico, and therefore Mexicans should be free to come and go as they please and do whatever they like regardless of the current government\u201d does not make sense to me. Add to that the fact that the current influx of illegal immigrants are primarily <i>not</i> Mexican...</div> </div> </div> </div>I did read that somewhere; that the recent surge of people aren't Mexican.<br /> A few years ago, California was seen as a &quot;failed state.&quot; With estimates that attribute illegal immigrants with 33%-50% of billions of its debt back then. (I'm aware that CA did balance its budget last year. But I don't think a lot of people are happy about how it was done.)<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, according to Hilary Clinton; <i>&quot;Canadian middle class incomes are now higher than in the United States. They are working fewer hours for more pay, \u2026 living longer on average, and facing less income inequality.&quot;</i> Considering how little Canada was affected by the Recession that the US and most other countries were, I guess this should come as no surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T21:04:35-07:00","id":189150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189144#post189144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did read that somewhere; that the recent surge of people aren't Mexican.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s worth noting that we have policies in place for returning Mexican nationals to Mexico (or Canadian nationals to Canada; but we don\u2019t seem to have much of an illegal immigration problem with Canadians pouring across our northern border), but out policies for illegal immigrants from non-contiguous countries make it very difficult to send them home. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189144#post189144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few years ago, California was seen as a &quot;failed state.&quot; With estimates that attribute illegal immigrants with 33%-50% of billions of its debt back then. (I'm aware that CA did balance its budget last year. But I don't think a lot of people are happy about how it was done.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can say that again. Governor Brown has done a patch job that has <i>temporarily</i> balanced the budget; but the fixes he put in place aren\u2019t sustainable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189144#post189144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated note, according to Hilary Clinton; <i>&quot;Canadian middle class incomes are now higher than in the United States. They are working fewer hours for more pay, \u2026 living longer on average, and facing less income inequality.&quot;</i> Considering how little Canada was affected by the Recession that the US and most other countries were, I guess this should come as no surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also explains the lack of Canadian refugees seeking to sneak into the US. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T21:21:18-07:00","id":189159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189144#post189144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated note, according to Hilary Clinton; <i>&quot;Canadian middle class incomes are now higher than in the United States. They are working fewer hours for more pay, \u2026 living longer on average, and facing less income inequality.&quot;</i> Considering how little Canada was affected by the Recession that the US and most other countries were, I guess this should come as no surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Math-wise this is because countries with social safety nets have smaller sections of the population at the extreme end of the poverty scale.<br /> <br /> And Canada was indeed significantly impacted by the global recession, what it didn't experience is as significantly a crash driven by the housing and commercial real estate bubbles the US had burst, instead merely suffering related effects from international bank arrangements. The other advantage of having more of the population in the middle class rather than on the edge of desperation is that the economy doesn't collapse in such downturns because it's not made of people running on the edge already. <a href=\"http://www.theglobeandmail.com/report-on-business/economy/economy-lab/why-canadas-recession-wasnt-as-brutal/article612437/\" target=\"_blank\">This </a>gives some of the reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189144#post189144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth noting that we have policies in place for returning Mexican nationals to Mexico (or Canadian nationals to Canada; but we don\u2019t seem to have much of an illegal immigration problem with Canadians pouring across our northern border), but out policies for illegal immigrants from non-contiguous countries make it very difficult to send them home.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mostly because arrangements with Canada and Mexico generally prevent the US from considering anyone from those countries to be refugees. They're considered enlightened and sensible folk where the government enforces just laws and therefor there would be no justification for someone to claim status as a refugee... which is where you get into the coast guard and navy practices of ensuring that people on the high seas seeking refuge in north america, get politely but firmly turned away before they stand a chance of making shore.<br /> <br /> Drat those people wanting a life free from torture and oppression coming to the country that spends billions every year to advertise itself as a beacon of freedom and a home to &quot;huddled masses yearning to be free&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T22:17:18-07:00","id":189203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189159#post189159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drat those people wanting a life free from torture and oppression coming to the country that spends billions every year to advertise itself as a beacon of freedom and a home to &quot;huddled masses yearning to be free&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself. I don\u2019t blame them for wanting to come here; I even understand why they\u2019re willing to pay human traffickers exhorbitant fees to sneak them into the country (fees which tend to wind up in the hands of drug cartels), given that the legal pipeline for getting here is hopelessly clogged and illegal entry still gets you most of the benefits that legal entry does (even though the laws on the books say that they shouldn\u2019t). I don\u2019t see it as a healthy situation, though; and something needs to be done to increase the flow of <i>legal</i> immigration while reducing the flow of <i>illegal</i> immigration.<br /> <br /> As I see it, that latter issue could be addressed three ways: increase border enforcement (which has been all but entirely neglected by the last two Presidential administrations), reduce the incentives for coming here illegally (such as cracking down on the employment of illegal immigrants), or reduce the incentives for leaving your home country (which amounts to nation-building, and isn\u2019t really practical; but if Mexico and Honduras didn\u2019t have massive problems with poverty and oppression, there wouldn\u2019t be as many people trying to leave).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the above quote is another example of what I was talking about before: it seeks to characterize anyone who has a problem with illegal immigration as heartless or stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-06-2014, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T23:29:50-07:00","id":189216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189203#post189203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, that latter issue could be addressed three ways: increase border enforcement (which has been all but entirely neglected by the last two Presidential administrations), reduce the incentives for coming here illegally (such as cracking down on the employment of illegal immigrants), or reduce the incentives for leaving your home country (which amounts to nation-building, and isn\u2019t really practical; but if Mexico and Honduras didn\u2019t have massive problems with poverty and oppression, there wouldn\u2019t be as many people trying to leave).</div> </div> </div> </div>Cracking down on employment for illegals would be more effective than anything else.<br /> <br /> Of course, as an IT worker, the people working out in the fields aren't my worry, it's the H1-Bs that companies ship in by the thousands to depress the wages here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:52:20-07:00","id":189352,"title":"","content":"There's a lot to hate in current US politics.<br /> The center position moved to the Right during Clinton's time in office. And so where did that leave the GOP after Clinton upstaged them on their own policies? Well they certainly weren't going to go Left. The Tea Party was a crank party back then, but became stronger during Clinton's tenure since many in the GOP started looking in their direction. And what can be said about Bush's term is probably better left unsaid. Punishing the Taliban in Afghanistan...needed to happen after 9/11. But the Iraq Debacle was a joke on an international scale.<br /> <br /> And then we have the current admin...<br /> Never was the rhetoric in pre-election speeches so grand, so hopeful...and after the election, such a damn disappointment. Not only did we get more of the same Bush in the way of foreign policies, but an increase in some of the worst excuses. We've got murders of American citizens without due process...in the name of the war on terror, innocent civilians getting killed...in the name of the war on terror (thereby pissing a lot of people off, and joining terrorist groups as a result), an admin that has increased the prosecution of whistleblowers, an increased lack of transparency, surveillance of US citizens without oversight, or for that matter any real justification (o..but there in print say it with me; &quot;in the name of the war on terror&quot; ).<br /> And a president that still believes in the ridiculous unproven concept of &quot;Free Trade.&quot; (I have to wonder if he wasn't some admirer of Ayn Rand at times) Like communism the idea looks great on paper. Sure did this president hash out Universal Health coverage? But only if it was profitable for Insurance companies. (and they helped write the law...like foxes taking over the henhouse) And they are having good year so far with profits soaring. And remember the banks that were &quot;Too big to fail?&quot; They're now about 40% bigger. Anti-Trust Laws are like most regulations, fading away.<br /> <br /> And among all the other rotten things politics have dumped on you, the American Taxpayer, the first audit ever of the Federal Reserve and it revealed <a href=\"http://www.forbes.com/sites/traceygreenstein/2011/09/20/the-feds-16-trillion-bailouts-under-reported/\" target=\"_blank\">$16 Trillion in bailouts</a> practically given away between GWB's and Obama's admins.<br /> <i>The findings verify that over $16 trillion was allocated to corporations and banks internationally, purportedly for \u201cfinancial assistance\u201d during and after the 2008 fiscal crisis. Sen. Bernie Sanders (I-VT); \u201cNo agency of the United States government should be allowed to bailout a foreign bank or corporation without the direct approval of Congress and the president.<br /> The Federal Reserve must be reformed to serve the needs of working families, not just CEOs on Wall Street.\u201d</i><br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> But I guess I can still vote right? Yeah, that'll work in a country where &quot;pay-to-play&quot; is the rule.<br /> Maybe I can write my congressman...and receive that nice formatted letter that says everything and nothing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:17:18-07:00","id":189442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189352#post189352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I guess I can still vote right? Yeah, that'll work in a country where &quot;pay-to-play&quot; is the rule. Maybe I can write my congressman...and receive that nice formatted letter that says everything and nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your choices are doing something small and actually participating in the process, or doing nothing but complaining somewhat passive-aggressively online and in no way participating in the process, I know which of the two options has the greater chance of success, however small that chance is. It is the option where you actually do something.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, since that swipe seems to be aimed at me, I will add that you seem to have missed the part of my suggestion in the other thread where I suggested you get other people involved. I'm not sure why you're acting as if I said you writing a single letter will change the world when I at least implied you'll need weight of numbers on your side unless you're doing so in order to be able to knock down a strawman, so please quit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T09:30:45-07:00","id":189482,"title":"","content":"Barely even started, and the fires have already started.<br /> <br /> History indicates the longer these threads go on, the more and more people can't think straight. We'll see how this one goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T10:17:27-07:00","id":189498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189203#post189203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the above quote is another example of what I was talking about before: it seeks to characterize anyone who has a problem with illegal immigration as heartless or stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, look: I'm coming from a place with a certain mental disability. And the reason I said that was because it never made sense to me logically. Could I have worded it much better? Probably definitely yes. But I also don't like you villainizing me either over something I said that I admit was stupid. I appreciate Nobody for keeping a cool head and trying to keep this thread civil.<br /> <br /> I had a best friend that came from a Mexican family when I was growing up, so the hatred directed towards them never made any sense to me. The United States is a country of immigrants.<br /> I usually see letters to the editor that complain about people speaking Spanish instead of English, without noting that there are legal Mexican immigrants who speak Spanish and English. If you get a book about California that has letters from a much earlier time, you can see still pro and con letters about illegal and legal immigration over Chinese immigrants.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'm fully aware that the current wave of illegal immigrants are not coming from Mexico. I've seen recent letters trying to blame the situation on Obama, rather than what is actually going on in countries like Guatemala, Honduras, and El Salvador. <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2014/06/13/us/children-immigrant-crisis/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naval Base in Ventura County is currently housing 204 children and expected to have 575. They are also trying to find the parents of these children first if they are within the United States.</a><br /> <br /> I will respectively bow out of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:26:26-07:00","id":189553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189203#post189203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the above quote is another example of what I was talking about before: it seeks to characterize anyone who has a problem with illegal immigration as heartless or stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun thing, refugee status isn't illegal immigration. It's perfectly legal and considered the correct and humanitarian thing to do.<br /> <br /> And then great efforts are taken to ensure that people desperate to get the country don't arrive. Again, perfectly legal to drive ships away from your territorial waters, even if the odds of them seeing land again anywhere are slim.<br /> <br /> It's not heartless, it's not stupid it's a set of hypocritical actions by the governments and very deliberate portrayal of the country. And is, if anything, somewhat worse than places like North Korea where the people are starving and dying and the leaders pronounce that everything is fine... The only ones being deceived are the leaders. Offering freedom and hope to desperate people around the world and then setting up military grade barriers around it to prevent legal access to it to akin to setting up an aide station offering free food and water in a starving county and stationing shoot-to-kill guards around it to keep people away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T14:05:30-07:00","id":189625,"title":"","content":"A random international observation.<br /> <br /> In Sweden we don't have a legal concept of &quot;illegal immigration&quot;. Instead we have the concept of &quot;Paperless&quot;. Paperless refers to the fact you lack the appropriate legal documentation to demonstrate your right to stay in the country, the cause of this is typically that either you haven't yet applied for immigrant/refugee status or you have been rejected. Legally this means you're allowed to stay in the country up to three months but you're not allowed to work (Working without residency or EU citizenship requires a special permit) however as of 2013 you're granted full right to medical care due to ethical concerns voiced by the hospitals.<br /> <br /> Another funny note is that there's a small swedish city S\u00f6dert\u00e4lje (65k inhabitants) that has accepted more Iraqi refugees that all of US combined and hosts the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assyriska_F%C3%B6reningen\" target=\"_blank\">Assyrian national soccer team</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 07-06-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:08:19-07:00","id":189729,"title":"","content":"In the US we have a very... strange way of processing &quot;paperless&quot; individuals int he hospital (to borrow Zironic's term and apply it somewhat incorrectly in this case). EMTALA, which was part of COBRA, in 1986 was our way of applying a blanket, &quot;everyone gets emergency room care, even if they can't pay,&quot; idea. The law then goes on to define what is emergency treatment, of course, and so we end up with a strange hodgepodge of who can and can't be thrown out of a hospital at what times.<br /> <br /> It's quite peculiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:12:26-07:00","id":189731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189442#post189442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your choices are doing something small and actually participating in the process, or doing nothing but complaining somewhat passive-aggressively online and in no way participating in the process, I know which of the two options has the greater chance of success, however small that chance is. It is the option where you actually do something.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, since that swipe seems to be aimed at me, I will add that you seem to have missed the part of my suggestion in the other thread where I suggested you get other people involved. I'm not sure why you're acting as if I said you writing a single letter will change the world when I at least implied you'll need weight of numbers on your side unless you're doing so in order to be able to knock down a strawman, so please quit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>JimB is absolutely right. Get involved in the process no matter how small. The problem most people seem to run into is they want change overnight and they want immediate satisfaction. Neither of which Congress was ever really designed to do. The House is somewhat more responsive than the Senate, but unless you're writing about something they have the authority to just handle, you are asking a couple hundred other ...*ahem* kind and generous souls *ahem* to have to agree with your Representative.<br /> <br /> Want to know the secret to changing Congress? The ultimate, no-shit it works secret? It's in your local elections and your state elections. The ones where only 6 people vote (hyperbolic statement). Those are the elections which affect the majority of Federal elections down the road. Most Congressmen don't get there by just buying the vote, contrary to what we say in the US. They get there through state and local elections first. They become a known commodity.<br /> <br /> Stop trying to change Congress tomorrow and start trying to change Congress in 10 to 15 years. Be in it for the long haul. You don't have much say over who goes to Congress in the election (but you DO have a say, don't get me wrong), but you do control who makes it that far, more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:16:01-07:00","id":189732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189352#post189352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a president that still believes in the ridiculous unproven concept of &quot;Free Trade.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Question for clarity: what's unproven about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure did this president hash out Universal Health coverage? But only if it was profitable for Insurance companies. </div> </div> </div> Honestly that was never the point of this law. Clinton's law in the 90s, it was, but not this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I guess I can still vote right? Yeah, that'll work in a country where &quot;pay-to-play&quot; is the rule. </div> </div> </div> See my post above.<br /> <br /> You seem like you're mad at a system you neither understand how to work or how it was designed. Since this is a politics discussion, I'm always happy to help with those two. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:27:07-07:00","id":189886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189442#post189442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your choices are doing something small and actually participating in the process, or doing nothing but complaining somewhat passive-aggressively online and in no way participating in the process, I know which of the two options has the greater chance of success, however small that chance is. It is the option where you actually do something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't really accomplished much in the national frame in the past 30 years or so, but if it makes you feel empowered, then go for it. I know someone that tries to vote third party. It never works out for one reason; money.) The process is far more effective at the local level. (All you have to do is look at homosexuality. There's nothing any administration can do from a legislative perspective. A federal constitutional amendment is dead upon arrival, and the Supreme Court has already had their say about federal level discrimination. And will likely continue that in the name of religion.<br /> Homosexuality from a politically point of view, hasn't been a winning issue. I think every prior congressional candidate that ran with it as a platform lost. And even now, 2014 players aren't likely to take it up. The states are far more ahead of the game.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189442#post189442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, since that swipe seems to be aimed at me, I will add that you seem to have missed the part of my suggestion in the other thread where I suggested you get other people involved. I'm not sure why you're acting as if I said you writing a single letter will change the world when I at least implied you'll need weight of numbers on your side unless you're doing so in order to be able to knock down a strawman, so please quit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Occupy Movement had numbers. And it scared the bejesus of those in DC. <a href=\"http://www.motherjones.com/politics/2013/06/nsa-spying-occupy-homeland-security\" target=\"_blank\">Federally coordinated crackdown</a> of a legitimate protest movement. Whatever lawsuits happened, were after the fact that it broke their momentum. Now their kept small, contained and controlled.<br /> <br /> Why does the fed giving $16 trillion out not bother anyone? Hmm...?<br /> <br /> Religion being used by for-profit corporations to deny contraceptive coverage should bother even the religious. Those that believe in secular law should be in a fury.<br /> If O'Connor had still been a judge (replaced by Alito) this would probably not have happened. It should not be seen as a coincidence that the three women judges were very opposed to this ruling.<br /> <br /> And why is it that the GOP, almost everyone of them, takes a dim (witted) view of science? Among other things Climate change is a reality that most of them don't believe in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  Link fix 07-06-2014, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T21:21:13-07:00","id":189909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189482#post189482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barely even started, and the fires have already started.<br /> <br /> History indicates the longer these threads go on, the more and more people can't think straight. We'll see how this one goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won\u2019t. I\u2019m not interested in butting heads with someone who thinks that I\u2019m dim-witted and who has the arrogance to tell me what should bother me; so I\u2019m bowing out now. If there was a chance that this might carry on as a civil conversation, I might continue to participate; but I really don\u2019t see a chance of that happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T21:30:16-07:00","id":189911,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the reasonable response, and good on you for choosing it.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I will have to count you as the thread's first victim.<br /> <br /> It's like watching a car wreck in slow motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer