I didn't pay any attention to it as it happened. It struck me as an impressive showing, but one that was wasted on a lost cause because the government could not afford to let the banks fail, as the result would have been economically catastrophic; and it also irritated me because hippies wearing masks of the face of an attempted mass murderer while dancing in the streets just get on my tits like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189886#post189886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the fed giving $16 trillion out not bother anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>It bothers a lot of people, but what alternative do you propose, and how do you think its effects would play out if it had been adopted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189886#post189886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Religion being used by for-profit corporations to deny contraceptive coverage should bother even the religious. Those that believe in secular law should be in a fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm far from happy with the ruling--my blasphemous response can be found in the appropriate thread--but speaking only for myself, if I'm going to start raging about religious law replacing secular law, I'm going to rage about the estimated 2,500 people ISIS made disappear in Iraq in the month of June for not being the correct sect of Islam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189886#post189886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why is it that the GOP, almost everyone of them, takes a dim (witted) view of science?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no way of answering that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T22:42:00-07:00","id":189935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189911#post189911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's the reasonable response, and good on you for choosing it.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I will have to count you as the thread's first victim.<br /> <br /> It's like watching a car wreck in slow motion.</div> </div> </div> </div>and this is taking too long..<br /> <br /> I'll start.<br /> <br /> YOU CAMEL MANNERED TUNIC WEARING MOLLYCODDLES!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-07-2014, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T22:42:40-07:00","id":189936,"title":"","content":"My biggest issue is the gerrymandering. In my last state election I had the choice of the far right Republican or the far, far right Tea Party candidate. There weren't any liberal candidates running because the district had been gerrymandered to the point that it was over 90% registered Republican.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T23:00:55-07:00","id":189941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189936#post189936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue is the gerrymandering. In my last state election I had the choice of the far right Republican or the far, far right Tea Party candidate. There weren't any liberal candidates running because the district had been gerrymandered to the point that it was over 90% registered Republican.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually something of a problem inherent in gerrymandering... in both directions, since at various times pretty much every political organization has done it.<br /> <br /> ... and actually, it might also tie into the question Shadowflame raised about GOP candidates and representatives.<br /> <br /> The more you manipulate your voter base to exclude anyone not likely to vote for you/your party the more your voter base is solidly on &quot;your&quot; side of the fence, as opposed to that other political party. It means that the general election is in the bag, there's no way that your party isn't going to win that area! Woohoo! Job Security! Except... it's not. You've now pushed the decision point back to the party candidate election. The are is going to be a win for the GOP for example, that's no longer in question, but the voters are still the voters, and whoever can make the better pitch and get the most votes based on what aspects of the GOP platform you want to push is the winner. So you're going to have candidates that are *solidly* promoting every plank of the platform they can.... and some of them go pretty far to the outside (again this is true in both parties).<br /> <br /> So you end up with candidates promoting views that to the broader general population can be questionable in an effort to grab the local outlying voters, and the whole set of ideas is heavily skewed in one direction or another to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T23:05:11-07:00","id":189944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189935#post189935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and this is taking too long..<br /> <br /> I'll start.<br /> <br /> YOU CAMEL MANNERED TUNIC WEARING MOLLYCODDLES!</div> </div> </div> </div>YOU FOP FACED FECAL FESTOONED FROLICKER!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T23:40:03-07:00","id":189969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189731#post189731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop trying to change Congress tomorrow and start trying to change Congress in 10 to 15 years. Be in it for the long haul.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there is a good point in there, there is also a significant problem:<br /> <br /> There are problems facing the USA that can't wait 10 to 15 years before we start the process of getting them solved 5-10 years after that. And I'm just talking about plain old practical things that really cannot wait that long (fixing infrastructure, stabilizing economy so it has more resilience, climate change). This isn't even getting into more moral/ethical/humanitarian issues that should not have to wait that long to get solved (though plenty of those issues impact things like stabilizing the economy).<br /> <br /> It's also a bit disrespctful to assume that just because someone is ranting about stuff on the Internet that they must not be involved in activism for their ideals at all. Or hasn't been at it for awhile.<br /> <br /> I've been involved with environmental activism for over 15 years... and it wasn't like I was starting up a movement. And it is really hard to convince new people to get into the long haul when you've been in the long haul for a decade and a half and politicians are still arguing over whether or not climate change is a problem; not even just arguing about how to fix it. There's almost no major political issue that doesn't have decades of activism behind it at this point. Trying to convince people to get in the trenches when Congress tends to swing back and forth around issues rather than actually move on them is really damned hard. &quot;Get involve in the long haul so you to can become cynical, jaded, and dismayed at politicians,&quot; is not an easy sell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T04:07:05-07:00","id":190122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189886#post189886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the fed giving $16 trillion out not bother anyone? Hmm...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it was either that or we redo the Great Depression with thousands of american citizens left penniless in the streets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T06:10:24-07:00","id":190202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189029#post189029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not that we\u2019re not aware of that fact as it is that we don\u2019t consider it to be particularly relevant to the current situation. \u201cCalifornia was once part of Mexico, and therefore Mexicans should be free to come and go as they please and do whatever they like regardless of the current government\u201d does not make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check my thinking: I recall a discussion once about policies that were being enacted in Arizona that were viewed as discriminatory toward U.S. citizens in the Latin American demographic who are a sizable proportion of the population of that state as a result of it having been a former Mexican territory, and how the arrangements for transferring ownership included the inhabitants of the time being given citizenship. The policy was seen as discriminatory for profiling according to terms that would also catch up and harass people of 100% U.S. American identity on the basis of what amounts to a physical similarity.<br /> <br /> Based on your responses, I gather that this isn't really the same thing, but I just wanted to straight up ask for clarity's sake.<br /> <br /> ... And maybe also extend a bit of a point that there are some anti-immigration policy implications where the relevance of certain States having formerly been Mexican property is pertinent, vis a vis the possibility of shoehorning Latin American citizens in with illegal immigrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T06:41:17-07:00","id":190225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189918#post189918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because ensuring that banks don't fold, and otherwise can continue to function whist charging a reasonable interest rate is exactly what the function of the federal reserve bank is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonable interest is &quot;near-zero interest?&quot; Well, like most here I would agree that such a percentage is very reasonable. I didn't have a problem bailing them out since I saw the reasoning. But the 16 trillion (I frankly find that number hard to grasp. Imagine what $1 trillion could do..) was doled out without anyone knowing about it. No public oversight. No accountability no nothing. That's wrong to me.<br /> <br /> These banking institutions committed all sorts of shenanigans and were &quot;too big to fail.&quot; And got bailed out on &quot;very reasonable&quot; loans. <a href=\"http://www.louisianaweekly.com/jpmorgan-chase-charged-with-making-predatory-loans-to-black-homeowners/\" target=\"_blank\">Joe Average succumbed to predatory loan practices</a> done by these same banks, and quickly gets foreclosed on since he can't afford the high interest payments anymore. How is this fair?<br /> <br /> You would think that the banks would have been more reasonable. Not going to happen though. Especially since the CEOs have to get their bonuses (<a href=\"http://money.cnn.com/2014/01/24/news/companies/dimon-pay/\" target=\"_blank\">JP Morgan CEO</a> got paid. One could reasonably say his continued employment was courtesy of Uncle Sam. Of course this is opposite of what is happening with <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2013/02/28/eu-banker-bonus-cap_n_2777427.html\" target=\"_blank\">European banks with bonuses getting slashed</a>)<br /> <br /> I should hope to read some agreement that &quot;Too Big To Fail&quot; is a problem. Because they're now a lot bigger, which means more political power. Breaking them up now (&quot;Anti-trust&quot; should have long kicked in before now) isn't possible.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gao.gov/new.items/d11696.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">GAO Report PDF</a> For those interested.<br /> <br /> And I'm running late...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T09:06:43-07:00","id":190386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=190225#post190225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reasonable interest is &quot;near-zero interest?&quot; Well, like most here I would agree that such a percentage is very reasonable. I didn't have a problem bailing them out since I saw the reasoning. But the 16 trillion (I frankly find that number hard to grasp. Imagine what $1 trillion could do..) was doled out without anyone knowing about it. No public oversight. No accountability no nothing. That's wrong to me.<br /> <br /> These banking institutions committed all sorts of shenanigans and were &quot;too big to fail.&quot; And got bailed out on &quot;very reasonable&quot; loans. <a href=\"http://www.louisianaweekly.com/jpmorgan-chase-charged-with-making-predatory-loans-to-black-homeowners/\" target=\"_blank\">Joe Average succumbed to predatory loan practices</a> done by these same banks, and quickly gets foreclosed on since he can't afford the high interest payments anymore. How is this fair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't confuse the billions used in the bank bailout with the trillions used by the reserve, it will only result in more mental suffering.<br /> <br /> You know how banks offer up loans to businesses and even major corporations? Be it something small like a few hundred thousand to open a new McDonalds or a few Billion to Texas Instruments to open a new manufacturing plant in the US? The reserve does much the same thing to the major banks. Technically it always has, but lately the numbers have been going up.<br /> <br /> This is something that had worked in a rather stable fashion for a very long time... and then it was decided that banks are the perfectly trustworthy bedrock, they don't need silly regulation and oversight, they can be self-regulating and more efficient for it. Then the headaches and the too-big-to-fail bailouts.<br /> <br /> Now technically a rather heavy chunk of the bailout monies were specifically set aside to deal with homeowner problems, it never really materialized as such. That's a thing that's being looked at. And as for the bailing out the banks when Joe Average gets shafted, if you don't save the bank first you're not going to have Joe Average getting screwed on his house, you're going to have hundreds of thousands in the same situation.<br /> <br /> The problem as I see it was the lack of follow-through down to actual relief for the homeowners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T09:57:13-07:00","id":190411,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm reading something wrong here, but it looks like you posted that banks don't need regulation...did you?<br /> Couldn't be...correct me if that's wrong please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:49:38-07:00","id":190480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=190411#post190411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm reading something wrong here, but it looks like you posted that banks don't need regulation...did you?<br /> Couldn't be...correct me if that's wrong please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry sarcasm. Banks *had* regulation, that was then removed under the claim that banks were perfectly fine to self-regulate. This was one of the key elements in them reaching the point of needing bail outs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:58:52-07:00","id":190821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189886#post189886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homosexuality from a politically point of view, hasn't been a winning issue. I think every prior congressional candidate that ran with it as a platform lost. And even now, 2014 players aren't likely to take it up. The states are far more ahead of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> So Barney Frank, Tammy Baldwin, Bob Filner, and Pete Stark all lost on that platform? Someone may want to tell them that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Occupy Movement had numbers. </div> </div> </div> Not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it scared the bejesus of those in DC. <a href=\"http://www.motherjones.com/politics/2013/06/nsa-spying-occupy-homeland-security\" target=\"_blank\">Federally coordinated crackdown</a> of a legitimate protest movement. Whatever lawsuits happened, were after the fact that it broke their momentum. Now their kept small, contained and controlled. </div> </div> </div> It's like the 60s... again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does the fed giving $16 trillion out not bother anyone? Hmm...? </div> </div> </div> It does bother me, but you're obviously ignoring me. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T16:32:56-07:00","id":190873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189969#post189969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While there is a good point in there, there is also a significant problem:<br /> <br /> There are problems facing the USA that can't wait 10 to 15 years before we start the process of getting them solved 5-10 years after that. And I'm just talking about plain old practical things that really cannot wait that long (fixing infrastructure, stabilizing economy so it has more resilience, climate change). This isn't even getting into more moral/ethical/humanitarian issues that should not have to wait that long to get solved (though plenty of those issues impact things like stabilizing the economy).<br /> <br /> It's also a bit disrespctful to assume that just because someone is ranting about stuff on the Internet that they must not be involved in activism for their ideals at all. Or hasn't been at it for awhile.<br /> <br /> I've been involved with environmental activism for over 15 years... and it wasn't like I was starting up a movement. And it is really hard to convince new people to get into the long haul when you've been in the long haul for a decade and a half and politicians are still arguing over whether or not climate change is a problem; not even just arguing about how to fix it. There's almost no major political issue that doesn't have decades of activism behind it at this point. Trying to convince people to get in the trenches when Congress tends to swing back and forth around issues rather than actually move on them is really damned hard. &quot;Get involve in the long haul so you to can become cynical, jaded, and dismayed at politicians,&quot; is not an easy sell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't intend disrespect by the statement.<br /> <br /> The problem I find with most activist groups is that they take too large a view of what they can change. As Tip put it, &quot;All politics is local.&quot; And it's very hard to get people to understand the system of systems nature of a federated government. It's creates obfuscated results that can be very hard to see where they came from for typical activists. Good on you for fighting that fight, whether or not your agree or disagree with me on any given political point.<br /> <br /> The thing about politics is that nothing can wait. Everything can't wait 10 to 15 years... when in reality, governments don't topple overnight and they don't make screaming comebacks overnight. They do it on a long, deliberative process. &quot;Climate change must be fixed right now!&quot; even though the best data we have says if we implemented all of the gas regulations the IPCC wants... we'd still see increases by 2100 and a barely measurable average decline from what the expected rise would be (I say again... decline from what the expected rise would be... decline of the rise...)<br /> <br /> So obviously it can wait another 5 to 10 years while we sort it out, barring a cascade effect that, if it's going to happen we have probably already caused and can't fix anyway. (This is not to say we should not fix the problem, merely that a problem of such catastrophic size won't get fixed in less than... a lifetime, perhaps.)<br /> <br /> &quot;Fix our infrastructure!&quot; Infrastructure was built over a great many years. Infrastructure is being quietly modernized, when it's not a hot button issue. Could we throw more money at it? Sure. But will that get us there faster? Past experience says no.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stabilize the economy!&quot; Boy howdy if we knew how to do that, it'd be a miracle.<br /> <br /> Usually the only thing you can move quickly on, and should move quickly on, are direct existential threats (war). The problem we sometimes have there is we move too fast on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T16:34:01-07:00","id":190876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=190386#post190386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't confuse the billions used in the bank bailout with the trillions used by the reserve, it will only result in more mental suffering.<br /> <br /> You know how banks offer up loans to businesses and even major corporations? Be it something small like a few hundred thousand to open a new McDonalds or a few Billion to Texas Instruments to open a new manufacturing plant in the US? The reserve does much the same thing to the major banks. Technically it always has, but lately the numbers have been going up.<br /> <br /> This is something that had worked in a rather stable fashion for a very long time... and then it was decided that banks are the perfectly trustworthy bedrock, they don't need silly regulation and oversight, they can be self-regulating and more efficient for it. Then the headaches and the too-big-to-fail bailouts.<br /> <br /> Now technically a rather heavy chunk of the bailout monies were specifically set aside to deal with homeowner problems, it never really materialized as such. That's a thing that's being looked at. And as for the bailing out the banks when Joe Average gets shafted, if you don't save the bank first you're not going to have Joe Average getting screwed on his house, you're going to have hundreds of thousands in the same situation.<br /> <br /> The problem as I see it was the lack of follow-through down to actual relief for the homeowners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fractional reserve banking is certainly a fun part of it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:37:45-07:00","id":190998,"title":"","content":"Hehe...too good not to post; <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2014/07/07/politics/scotus-judge-blogger/index.html?hpt=hp_t2\" target=\"_blank\">Blogging jurist to Supreme Court: 'STFU'</a><br /> <i><br /> The Supreme Court is used to having its decisions publicly criticized, but rarely in R-rated language spouted by a federal judge, who says the justices should just &quot;stfu.&quot; The remarks come from Nebraska-based Judge Richard Kopf, who has a reputation for provocative commentary on his <a href=\"http://HerculesandtheUmpire.com.\" target=\"_blank\">personal blog</a>.<br /> Kopf, an appointee of President George H.W. Bush, criticized the high court's ruling last week in the so-called &quot;<a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2014/06/30/politics/scotus-obamacare-contraception/index.html?iref=allsearch\" target=\"_blank\">Hobby Lobby</a>&quot; case.<br /> <br /> &quot;Five male Justices of the Supreme Court, who are all members of the Catholic faith and who each were appointed by a President who hailed from the Republican party, decided that a huge corporation, with thousands of employees and gargantuan revenues, was a 'person' entitled to assert a religious objection to the Affordable Care Act's contraception mandate because that corporation was 'closely held' by family members,&quot; he wrote. &quot;To the average person, the result looks stupid and smells worse.&quot;<br /> And he went further. &quot;Next term is the time for the Supreme Court to go quiescent-- this term and several past terms has proven that the court is now causing more harm (division) to our democracy than good by deciding hot button cases that the court has the power to avoid. As the kids say, it is time for the Court to stfu.&quot;</i><br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> I can only <img src=\"http://www.kurts-smilies.de/applaus.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T19:46:16-07:00","id":191036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=190873#post190873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't intend disrespect by the statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't stop the tone from being disrespectful. Nor the continued assumption that you understand things better than other people just because they aren't phrasing things too your liking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem I find with most activist groups is that they take too large a view of what they can change. </div> </div> </div>Most? Or just most you've got experience with?<br /> <br /> I belong to a group the promotes planting and maintaining native wild fields near agricultural sites. It's entirely local. We're after both supporting local wildlife and decreasing the local impact of fertilizers, pesticides (and it turns out colony collapse disorder with bees). We're not after any sort of federal change. Because we don't need the government to do anything. Though grants are nice.<br /> <br /> Most of us are also part of larger groups that you're more used to thinking of as being too naive. But it isn't that we're naive. It's that there are local problems and their are larger problems. We need local activism and federal activism.<br /> <br /> The bees are actually a good example of this. On one hand there's a huge amount of simple local things we can do about bees. And we really need them. But at the same time there is a national crisis here. If bee colonies continue to drop the impact on the agricultural industry is immense. We'll need to start paying people to pollinate crops, vastly increasing the price of food just to maintain current production levels.<br /> <br /> Local activism can help, a lot, but this is a problem that doesn't end at any line drawn on a map. The few counties that have managed to start repairing the damage done to bee populations can't magically replace all the colonies we've lost. They can't fix the problems that caused the collapse in the first place. That's why we also need better regulations on monocultures crops field distributions (monocultures are problematic, but the bigger problem is that we have giant fields of them that aren't broken up by other crops), and chemical applications over biological ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about politics is that nothing can wait. </div> </div> </div>That might be how politicians approach their issues of choice... but there are plenty of things that can wait. I'm pretty sure naming something else after someone can wait even if that gets done without much fuss.<br /> <br /> Tax code reform should get done... but it can wait. We'll collect taxes even if we're doing it in a suboptimal way.<br /> <br /> I think it is incredibly dangerous to just see it as, &quot;well in politics nothing can wait, so everything is equal,&quot; when in reality this simply isn't the case. Even if the country isn't going to get destroyed if infrastructure issues aren't addressed or climate change doesn't get acted on overnight, it doesn't mean we aren't digging ourselves so deep by not fixing it that we aren't heading to the point where &quot;fixing&quot; stops being the point and &quot;coping with the complete loss of something and trying to manage what to do&quot; is the new issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So obviously it can wait another 5 to 10 years while we sort it out, barring a cascade effect that, if it's going to happen we have probably already caused and can't fix anyway. (This is not to say we should not fix the problem, merely that a problem of such catastrophic size won't get fixed in less than... a lifetime, perhaps.) </div> </div> </div>The problem is we are, going by the best science on the subject, on that point where if we don't start doing things now, not in 10 years, then we're going to get into cascade effects that we can't stop. We're already seeing the opening signs of those cascades getting set off. Politics has spent decades not doing enough when doing it would have been easier and we wouldn't be stuck in a situation of picking how bad do we want it.<br /> <br /> This sort of attitude is one of the reasons why climate change isn't moving. If you don't want to sound like denialist and just claim it doesn't matter, you can throw up your hands and say, &quot;well it's too late, so screw it.&quot; The longer we wait, the worse fixing it gets, until fixing it isn't an option any more and the slow death of larger nations starts setting in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Stabilize the economy!&quot; Boy howdy if we knew how to do that, it'd be a miracle. </div> </div> </div>Even if not completely universally effective, there's plenty of prominent economic thinkers both outside of politics and inside of it that have solid proposals to do this. For example, it isn't going to fix everything, but eliminating the student debt bloating would certainly help stabilize the economy. I don't know any economic principle that says this problem is not a problem, or that fixing it will make it worse. Everything I've read on it says pretty universally that<br /> <br /> The inability to prioritize issues by need and immediacy is a problem. And it doesn't have to be one. Waiting inherently means there are major issues that are going to get worse - possibly to the point of not being able to be fixed - so telling people that they have to suck it up and wait ~20 years before starting to fix it will even happen is basically just acknowledging that our system is going to drive itself off a cliff because we can't decided to apply brakes fast enough for anything that isn't war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T20:18:48-07:00","id":191055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=190876#post190876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fractional reserve banking is certainly a fun part of it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>A more fundamental component, and something that I disagree with myself... the problem is that it is an advantage. So let's say the government of the US said &quot;nope, no more fractional reserve issues&quot; (which I consider slightly less likely than the sun exploding tomorrow), they can only enforce it on US banks or at best on US held assets. It's become an international standard, so besides the relative ease of shifting assets around on paper to make it work on paper, it results in a non-level playing field against the banks that *do* follow such a policy or law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T22:42:26-07:00","id":191132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=189944#post189944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YOU FOP FACED FECAL FESTOONED FROLICKER!</div> </div> </div> </div>YOU CHEEKY GABBING TRIPE SPREADING MUPPET!<br /> <br /> seriously, I may have to recruit Raven into this. My Old English insults are a bit rusty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avata