from non-Middle East oil producers is larger than whatever US of A now imports from ME. USA imports more from Canada than any ME country.<br /> <br /> Oil-dependency is a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.... ish.<br /> <br /> The reason we keep using middle eastern oil for stuff is that it's a very very light grade oil. Makes it a lot easier and far more profitable to produce the highest grades of fuels from it. It's also part of the whole global supply, if it dries up prices go up from that dramatically. So like everything that the media likes to turn black and white it isn't. The US doesn't suddenly grind to a halt if all of the middle east suddenly stopped producing oil, but the cost of jet fuel will go up significantly and the spiking global prices would have a significant impact in the US. Cars are not suddenly going to be abandoned in the road because we turned into a Mad Max world of no gasoline, but it means it would quickly go up in price as demand outpaced supply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=198934#post198934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Estimates from 2012 I found say USA would become top oil producer in 2017.<br /> <br /> Now that shale oil is actually profitable to exploit, USA is intensifying its production.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are side effects from the shale oil production (as always everything has a catch) but it also tends to be of a heavier grade.<br /> <br /> <br /> The ready availability of heavier grade oil is one of the reasons why I really wish the US/Canada would get behind the newer generations of diesel engines for vehicles, easier to make fuel with good efficiency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:03:09-07:00","id":199083,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=198928#post198928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you know, USA's domestic oil production combined with imports from non-Middle East oil producers is larger than whatever US of A now imports from ME. USA imports more from Canada than any ME country.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* But businesses run the show politically. That's why the oil doesn't stay here where we all want it on the cheap. It gets shipped to other countries that pay more for it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=198928#post198928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oil-dependency is a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if that were true. Imagine say, the US no longer needs oil. What do you think would happen as a result when the biggest consumer suddenly is no longer in play? (Re: Petrol-dollars versus Petro-Euros)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:37:20-07:00","id":199352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=198934#post198934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Estimates from 2012 I found say USA would become top oil producer in 2017.<br /> <br /> Now that shale oil is actually profitable to exploit, USA is intensifying its production.</div> </div> </div> </div>Derp, sorry. My response was to Shadowflame. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:38:57-07:00","id":199357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=199083#post199083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *nods* But businesses run the show politically. That's why the oil doesn't stay here where we all want it on the cheap. It gets shipped to other countries that pay more for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> If we didn't sell it on the global market, it would just drive the price of oil up further, so not sure where the complaint is here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:34:44-07:00","id":199397,"title":"","content":"The biggest consumer would just be self-sufficient, Shadowflame. I don't think we will run out of oil completely in nearest future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:16:08-07:00","id":200183,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=199397#post199397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest consumer would just be self-sufficient, Shadowflame. I don't think we will run out of oil completely in nearest future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe your thinking this through. (That why I re; petro-dollars vs petro-euros) Biggest consumer is the biggest buyer...and the most money in circulation. And that money gets taken out of play. And that's just thinking a little outside the box. Whole economies are based upon oil consumption (Part of the &quot;resource-based economies&quot; that some countries have). If that goes away you can count on a global Depression (and worse), socio-political instabilities in many countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T04:42:50-07:00","id":201011,"title":"","content":"If people stop buying oil from Middle East and they suffer from economic recession in result, I won't pity them since countries like Saudi Arabia are opressive dictatorships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T05:14:22-07:00","id":201020,"title":"","content":"Many are, but by no means all. Egypt, Russia and the UAE are among the worlds top 5 exporters of crude petroleum, and they tend to be pretty good as governments go, albeit hardly problem-free, but not oppressive dictatorships. Also Qatar, Oman and Azerbaijan are all from that broad part of the world, are major oil producers, and aren't dictatorships, albeit they do tend to have a bit of a chequered past. And recessions, like really, really bad ones, are more likely to create dictatorships than they are to remove them, so even on that basis it doesn't help.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there's the problem that economic troubles hit the people in charge <i>last</i> in a situation like that, which means you'd be looking at literally thousands of people dying before the dictators, such as they are, even begin to be even remotely concerned. Unless there's some kind of armed revolution, and that rarely ends well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 07-18-2014, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T16:11:14-07:00","id":203293,"title":"","content":"So the plane went down and apparently most of the nations are content with sending angry letters while site is being looted.<br /> <br /> &quot;fun&quot; world we live in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T17:15:24-07:00","id":203314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=203293#post203293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the plane went down and apparently most of the nations are content with sending angry letters while site is being looted.<br /> <br /> &quot;fun&quot; world we live in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody at the crash site even knows what the heck they should be doing or where things should be done. Bodies are being sent to morgues and investigations on the pro-russian side, and the same on the Ukrainian side. It's trying to recover stuff from a war zone, never an easy or good task, made worse by the heavy politics going on right now. <br /> <br /> Until further confirmation or evidence is actually available things are still up in the air politically, and frankly nobody wants to push it too hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:54:24-07:00","id":203397,"title":"","content":"The EU is still trying to get on it's feet economically, and they have a lot of love for Russian oil, especially Germany. They prod that bear too much and they may find their collective economic rug pulled out from under their feet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:39:14-07:00","id":205434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=203314#post203314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody at the crash site even knows what the heck they should be doing or where things should be done. Bodies are being sent to morgues and investigations on the pro-russian side, and the same on the Ukrainian side. It's trying to recover stuff from a war zone, never an easy or good task, made worse by the heavy politics going on right now.<br /> <br /> Until further confirmation or evidence is actually available things are still up in the air politically, and frankly nobody wants to push it too hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pushing too hard with Russia could push them into China's arms while we're pushing other actions with China. Pushing to hard with China could do the same thing for Russia. The Commander of SAC put out an interesting article in the quarterly Defense Review magazine where he talks about actions the US can take to try to keep one of those two allied with the US and prevent a Sino-Soviet re-emergence that could be, frankly, devastating to the US and EU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T05:57:01-07:00","id":205969,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile Israel has gone to Hell. Well, Israel was going there anyway. kinda screwy that the local news glossed over the 120+Palestinian children killed in 2 days, but spent plenty of time speaking of the &quot;brave sacrifices&quot; made by the Israeli military of the dozen or so Israeli soldiers killed so far, probably in skirmishes... with the parents of the children they just butchered...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/middleeast/israel/10984451/Israels-offensive-in-Gaza-has-killed-more-children-than-fighters-say-human-rights-groups.html\" target=\"_blank\">Israel's offensive in Gaza has 'killed more children than fighters'</a><br /> <i><br /> More children than Palestinian fighters are being killed in the offensive on Gaza, according to the latest United Nations statistics, despite Israel's claims to be waging a targeted military campaign.<br /> Gaza's health ministry said that 580 Palestinians had been killed, including 155 children.<br /> The UN's Office for the Co-ordination of Humanitarian Affairs, said that, as of Tuesday morning, 149 children had been killed, compared with 87 confirmed members of armed groups. Even including unconfirmed combatant deaths, more children would still have died.<br /> The Palestinian monitoring group Al Mezan Centre for Human Rights has given The Telegraph the names of 132 of the dead, all under the age of 18.<br /> In addition, Save the Children said almost a third of those injured were children. Less than a quarter of all casualties are thought to be Hamas militants. </i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/middleeast/palestinianauthority/10984259/Revealed-the-Palestinian-children-killed-by-Israeli-forces.html\" target=\"_blank\">Graph</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:56:22-07:00","id":207717,"title":"","content":"This is not meant to be callous but... what do you think happens to children in war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T05:58:06-07:00","id":211126,"title":"","content":"Hint, Palestinian paramilitary organisations kill children too when they fire their rockets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T06:35:41-07:00","id":211149,"title":"","content":"It's called &quot;ethnic cleansing.&quot; But since <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/207354-emperor-for-a-day?p=211122#post211122\">you think the world is fine as it is</a>...(and targeting children on a beach? Only a couple of little kids on a beach...wtf?)<br /> <br /> Its intent is not to kill all Palestinians. That'd force the US government and EU governments to stop subsidizing , arming, trading with and politically supporting Israel. Its intent is to take what worthwhile land it hasn't taken already and crush any resistance using massive military superiority. The Israeli government and military are not at all averse to targeting civilians to punish those dirty Arabs though as long as they can do it in a way that avoids losing US support.<br /> <br /> And that Hamas/Hezbollah/Fatah got those civilians killed by using them as &quot;human shields&quot; line is 95% bullshit every time too. The Israeli military and government said it in 'Operation Defensive Shield' in Jenin and Nablus in 2002 - <a href=\"http://inplaceoffear.blogspot.co.uk/2009/02/there-were-israeli-war-crimes-in-jenin.html\" target=\"_blank\">human Rights Watch, Amnesty and B'TSelem between them found that in fact Israeli forces bulldozed Palestinian homes with the people living in them inside them, shot civilians including disabled people in the street and targeted ambulances and paramedics trying to get in to help the wounded. On top of that they made Palestinian civilians walk in front of them at gunpoint as human shields themselves</a>.<br /> <br /> In the 2006 Lebanon war the Israelis claimed Hezbollah were using civilians as human shields by firing rockets from villages, causing Israeli return fire to kill civilians. Human Rights Watch <a href=\"http://www.hrw.org/reports/2007/lebanon0907/3.htm\" target=\"_blank\">investigated it and found out that was bullshit too - the Hezbollah rocket fire was coming from emplacements in the hills many miles from the villages like Qana which the Israelis hit</a>. The Israelis also <a href=\"http://www.refworld.org/cgi-bin/texis/vtx/rwmain?page=country&amp;category=&amp;publisher=HRW&amp;type=&amp;coi=ISR&amp;rid=&amp;docid=45d1705f2&amp;skip=0\" target=\"_blank\">bombed lots of clearly marked ambulances with lights , sirens etc all across Lebanon</a> - and tried to focus on one single case claiming it was a &quot;hoax&quot; - but <a href=\"http://www.hrw.org/reports/2006/12/19/hoax-wasn-t\" target=\"_blank\">HRW proved even that one was no hoax</a>.<br /> <br /> Human Rights Watch <a href=\"http://www.hrw.org/sites/default/files/reports/ioptwf0809webwcover_1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">found multiple cases of Israeli forces shooting unarmed civilians that they could see clearly dead where no fighting was taking place at the time too</a>.<br /> <br /> And you know how many Israeli soldiers have since been jailed for the 700 odd Palestinian civilians killed in Cast Lead ? Two. One <a href=\"http://www.ynetnews.com/articles/0,7340,L-3760488,00.html\" target=\"_blank\">for 7 months for taking a credit card</a>. And the other was <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-middle-east-19243246\" target=\"_blank\">45 days for &quot;illegal discharge of a weapon&quot;</a> (into a Palestinian woman).<br /> <br /> And even when there's no conflict going on Israeli forces <a href=\"http://www.duncanmcfarlane.org/Israel-Palestine/notdemocratsversusterrorists/#_ftn1\" target=\"_blank\">regularly shoot unarmed Palestinian children and teenagers dead</a> - sometimes when they're in school or at home or playing the street, other times when they're throwing stones at Israeli troops or protesting against the occupation.<br /> <br /> They shot <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/may/22/footage-palestinian-boys-shot-genuine-btselem\" target=\"_blank\">two unarmed 16 year old Palestinians</a> dead <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/jun/12/autopsy-palestinian-teenager-wounds-consistent-live-ammunition\" target=\"_blank\">with live ammunition in the West Bank in May</a> for protesting against the Nakba ('disaster) in May - and <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/jul/25/palestinian-protests-continue-israel-considers-ground-operation-ceasefire\" target=\"_blank\">another 16 year old</a> is among the <a href=\"http://www.smh.com.au/world/palestinian-toll-tops-1000-as-israel-ceasefire-called-to-recover-gaza-dead-20140727-zxcdw.html\" target=\"_blank\">8 people they've shot dead (and 250 wounded) in the West Bank since Palestinians there began protesting</a> against the Israeli attacks on schools, hospitals and family homes in Gaza in the last few days.<br /> <br /> And how are Hamas or Fatah or Islamic Jihad going to committ another Holocaust in Israel by the way when thousands and thousands of rockets in the last month killed just two Israeli civilians (<a href=\"http://www.timesofisrael.com/negev-bedouin-defenseless-as-man-killed-4-injured-by-gaza-rocket/\" target=\"_blank\">one a Bedouin Arab because the government doesnt provide them with bomb shelters)</a> while the Israeli military has thousands of tanks and heavy artillery pieces, drones, F16s etc?<br /> <br /> And if they want to weaken Hamas why hasn't Israel given Palestinians a viable state, which would collapse support for Hamas - they could even have given it in negotiations solely with President Abbas of Fatah, which would have rocketed support for Fatah and made Hamas has beens. Instead they've punished the entire population of Gaza with blockade and bombing, which increases support for Hamas. Seems the Israeli government must like that war with Gaza much more than they like a peace deal - it's ridiculously easy to win, having Hamas there is great PR for Israel and it lets them keep attention from their annexation of the whole West Bank.<br /> <br /> It's no wonder that Israel is compared to Nazi Germany.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  Clarification 07-28-2014, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:46:49-07:00","id":211862,"title":"","content":"I say again, what do you think happens to children in war?<br /> <br /> Oh and I was unaware that I'm fine with the world as is... please continue to enlighten me as to how I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:00:44-07:00","id":211871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NOBODY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh and I was unaware that I'm fine with the world as is... please continue to enlighten me as to how I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm. Exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times ne