ame":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T21:08:11-07:00","id":213132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=212867#post212867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you don't seem to be terribly interested in dialogue, just posting somebody else's opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody, I hope you know I got nothing against you, but even so, it's very frustrating to try to have an opinion-based dialogue with you, since you refuse to express your own opinions on anything more serious than which edition of Exalted you prefer. As such, I really can't blame Shadowflame for not sharing with you an opinion you won't return. Hell, I think he deserves a round of applause for backing up all his assertions with citations the way he did. Say what you want about his conclusions, but the work he did to get there was thorough and conscientious. That's not nothing; that's something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T12:00:18-07:00","id":213806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=213035#post213035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, it may be too late to change what's going on. The war is quickly escalating to an existential crisis for Hamas.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you say that? As far as I can tell this war is great for Hamas. They're getting more support then ever. Meanwhile the only thing preventing international sanctions against Israel (The united states) looks less happy by the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T15:00:04-07:00","id":213971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=213132#post213132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody, I hope you know I got nothing against you, but even so, it's very frustrating to try to have an opinion-based dialogue with you, since you refuse to express your own opinions on anything more serious than which edition of Exalted you prefer. As such, I really can't blame Shadowflame for not sharing with you an opinion you won't return. Hell, I think he deserves a round of applause for backing up all his assertions with citations the way he did. Say what you want about his conclusions, but the work he did to get there was thorough and conscientious. That's not nothing; that's something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen assertions. I've seen regurgitation of other people's opinions.<br /> <br /> For a rare moment, I will dip into what is PURELY opinion and speculation on my part: based on the context of earlier conversations with him, I don't think he used citations to get to his conclusion. I think he had a conclusion and cherry picked his sources to back up from it. But I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2058,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","user":"Nobody","date":". 07-30-2014, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T15:05:04-07:00","id":213978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=213806#post213806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you say that? As far as I can tell this war is great for Hamas. They're getting more support then ever. Meanwhile the only thing preventing international sanctions against Israel (The united states) looks less happy by the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you see in the media isn't representative of what we, the US, are actually doing. I sit next to the Foreign Military Sales desk (specifically the Israel desk). Hamas is getting more recruits than ever, don't take that to mean they can actually win or do anything more than aggravate the situation further. The problem is that Israel is slowly ratcheting up the response as the original intent was, &quot;crush Hamas' military capabilities so they can't strike back.&quot;<br /> <br /> To do that, the mission is growing, and growing, and growing... and will eventually turn to a war of existence for Hamas. Israel is in no danger of losing their international support (arms and equipment) right now, despite what CNN says. The UN can't really do anything to them right now as any such action goes through the security council and guess who has a veto vote on that council.<br /> <br /> Let us still hope level heads prevail on both sides. It would help if Israel's responses were more proportional at this point (though I can see why they're not, as that hasn't been working)... it would also help if Hamas stopped breaking ceasefires early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T16:08:04-07:00","id":214005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=213978#post213978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you see in the media isn't representative of what we, the US, are actually doing. I sit next to the Foreign Military Sales desk (specifically the Israel desk). Hamas is getting more recruits than ever, don't take that to mean they can actually win or do anything more than aggravate the situation further. The problem is that Israel is slowly ratcheting up the response as the original intent was, &quot;crush Hamas' military capabilities so they can't strike back.&quot;<br /> <br /> To do that, the mission is growing, and growing, and growing... and will eventually turn to a war of existence for Hamas. Israel is in no danger of losing their international support (arms and equipment) right now, despite what CNN says. The UN can't really do anything to them right now as any such action goes through the security council and guess who has a veto vote on that council.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not actually possible for Israel to eliminate Hamas through millitary force short of complete genocide of Gaza. Israel would not as a state survive genocide of Gaza. There will never be any such thing as a war of existence for Hamas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T16:54:19-07:00","id":214024,"title":"","content":"I agree with the first sentence, and the second, but not with the third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T17:14:19-07:00","id":214057,"title":"","content":"So Representative Rothfus and Woodall are on the House floor right now talking about the bills stuck in the Senate and how the Senate won't act. 300 some bills stuck in the Senate... I'm wondering if they do know that some of them are stuck int he Senate because of their own party (no judgment of Republicans or Democrats, just musing at the hilarity of Washington: city of speak out of both sides of your mouth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T20:51:50-07:00","id":217143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=214057#post214057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm wondering if they do know that some of them are stuck int he Senate because of their own party (no judgment of Republicans or Democrats, just musing at the hilarity of Washington: city of speak out of both sides of your mouth).</div> </div> </div> </div>The one that took the cake in my mind was when they were debating military action in Syria, Senator Rubio argued <i>vehemently</i> in favor of military action and lambasted Obama for not doing enough for something like half an hour -- and then voted <i>against</i> the authorization just to shaft him. They know. They just don't care.<br /> <br /> On the Gaza Strip thing, I think pretty much everybody looks like a turd-pile here. Hamas is very cynically doing its best to goad the Israelis into causing civilian casualties. The Israelis are exacerbating things by not really caring if they cause collateral casualties. The Palestinians at large are politically backing up Hamas -- which only eggs them on. And we (the U.S.) are running interference for the Israelis at the U.N.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the biggest issue at work here has nothing whatsoever to do with the Palestinians, but rather the internal politics of both the United States and Israel. The U.S. could probably force an end to this whole nightmare if we could muster the political willpower to use our economic and political influence. Gaza is a chaotic nightmare, but the settlement issue in the West Bank is more clear-cut (against Israel), and ultimately easier to resolve. There is <i>absolutely</i> no legal justification for those settlements, and they're causing all sorts of international headaches for us (because of our support of Israel). What burns me is that jerks like Netanyahu <i>wouldn't have a country </i>if it wasn't for us, but anytime we start pushing them on the issue, they show us nothing but a really disgusting level of disrespect (the Kinesset's statements regarding SecState Kerry lately are a good example). If they really want to hold to the line that we're trying to interfere in their internal affairs, then fine. We should cut off all of their financial and military support. Let's see just how long that attitude lasts. It isn't going to happen, though. AIPAC will <i>never</i> allow funding to Israel to be curtailed or support for them at the U.N. to be rescinded, and the domestic political situation here is so fractious right now, that even the Obama Administration acknowledges that it's not going to try to fight that one again.<br /> <br /> Over in Israel, however they have their own political problems. I think even the majority of the Israelis have figured out that none of this is sustainable. What to do, is another matter, however. I sort of get the impression that even they would like to put an end to West Bank settlement, but they have their <i>own</i> crazies, and just like <i>our</i> wing-nuts, theirs <i>vote</i>. That Hamas and Hezbollah are quite fond of pushing buttons on the Israelis, is not helpful (not that any of that lot care).<br /> <br /> Finally, there's the real problem of the Gaza Strip: Namely that it's essentially one big refugee camp resulting from the various wars that the Israelis had to fight in the 40s and 50s (and to a lesser extent, 60s). All of those people (and much of Hezbollah's base in Lebanon) were evicted as part of military operations. It was theoretically supposed to be temporary. Under international law, you cannot just displace civilians simply because you covet their lands (a somewhat ironic point given that early support for Israel was a reaction due to what the Nazis did). If the Israelis ever want a lasting peace, as a legal matter, they're going to have to figure out what to do with all the displaced civilians. They can't just leave them locked up in the Gaza Strip and in southern Lebanon.<br /> <br /> None of this even touches on other lesser (but still thorny) issues like water rights or free-transit between Gaza and the West Bank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-09-2014, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T22:14:37-07:00","id":217179,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2014/07/israel-provoked-this-war-109229.html?ml=po_r#.U9b0txFOUdU\" target=\"_blank\">Israel Provoked This War</a><br /> <br /> Israeli officials <a href=\"http://nymag.com/daily/intelligencer/2014/07/hamas-didnt-kidnap-the-israeli-teens-after-all.html\" target=\"_blank\">knew all along</a> that Hamas was not behind the kidnapping which was the pretext for the latest round of fighting.<br /> <br /> Of course since that cat is out of the bag, Bibi <a href=\"http://www.politico.com/story/2014/08/netanyahu-to-us-dont-second-guess-me-on-hamas-109664.html?hp=l5\" target=\"_blank\">tells Obama admin</a> &quot;not to ever second guess me again&quot; <i>on the matter.<br /> The officials also said Netanyahu said he should be &quot;trusted&quot; on the issue and about the unwillingness of Hamas to enter into and follow through on cease-fire talks.</i><br /> <br /> Hmf..I guess he want to give the US orders..and ignore the facts and support his little murder spree.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/jul/31/gaza-faces-precipice-death-toll-tops-1400\" target=\"_blank\">Gaza 'faces precipice' as death toll passes 1,400</a><br /> <br /> <i>The death toll in Gaza has topped 1,400, with more than 40 people dying after another day of intense Israeli bombardment from air, sea and land.<br /> <br /> The toll is now greater than in both previous rounds of fighting between Israel and Hamas. Israeli military losses are also significantly higher.<br /> <br /> Palestinian officials in Gaza said on Thursday that 8,200 people had been wounded in the four-week operation. Up to 80% of the Palestinian casualties were civilians, according to local non-government organisations and the UN.<br /> <br /> Three civilians on the Israeli side and 56 soldiers have been killed so far.</i><br /> <br /> Imteresting; <a href=\"http://www.globalpost.com/dispatch/news/regions/americas/140730/latin-american-recall-ambassadors-israel-gaza\" target=\"_blank\">Why Latin American diplomats are pulling out of Israel</a><br /> <br /> <i>Latin American nations are expressing their revulsion at the bloodshed in Gaza \u2014 and squarely pinning the blame on Israel.<br /> <br /> Chile, Peru and El Salvador said this week they are recalling their ambassadors from Israel for consultation. That was after Ecuador and Brazil did the same last week. And on Wednesday, Bolivian President Evo Morales declared Israel a \u201cterrorist state.\u201d<br /> Lots of world leaders have denounced the violence on both sides of Israel\u2019s 3-week-old war against Hamas in Gaza. Palestinian casualties have <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/31/world/middleeast/israel-gaza.html\" target=\"_blank\">reached 1,328</a>, according to Gaza health authorities, while the Israeli death toll is close to 60.<br /> But the Latin Americans appear to be leading a diplomatic storm, flying envoys out of Tel Aviv.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T11:51:12-07:00","id":217545,"title":"","content":"Well, in the article you cited, there is some truth and some falsehoods. They're right that the underlying issue at stake is the status quo in Gaza is not sustainable. Gaza is the legacy of the refugee camps resulting from several rounds of forced relocations decades ago. The Strip just cannot support the population that lives there. Unfortunately, the politics are a little more complicated. The Palestinian election in 2006 (I think it was) was a disaster in that it established Hamas as the legitimate power in Gaza. Hamas has always been a terrorist organization, and that's how the whole organization thinks. The assertion that Israel instigated the latest round of fighting is true in a sense because of how far they've backed the Palestinians into a corner, but their purpose in the blockade was to force Hamas to relinquish control of Gaza to the Palestinian Authority. The idea that Hamas was somehow innocent in all this is totally false. The existence of all the attack tunnels is proof of that. THAT was the real reason that the Israelis attacked -- to destroy the tunnels, and to a lesser extent, to &quot;mow the grass&quot; with regard to Hamas' other capabilities. What was the central issue that led to the cease-fire collapsing? The Israelis continued to mine the tunnels in the areas that they controlled. Even Hamas admitted that.<br /> As to the huge numbers of civilian casualties, I think Hamas is a little bit to blame (they're profiting politically big-time from the body count), but I think that's really more of a practical issue on both sides. Gaza is so tightly packed that there's no place for the civilian population to evacuate to, and besides Hamas HAS to seek concealment among the civilian population since they'll be slaughtered if they were to separate themselves from the civvies (sort of disreputable, but it's a necessity). On the other hand, the Israelis probably aren't actively trying to cause civilian casualties, but if they know that a rocket attack (as an example) came from a particular location, they're not really required to tiptoe around either.<br /> There's no real good solution here because if Hamas were to simply give up and pursue a diplomatic course, nothing would happen. What really needs to happen is the United States needs to start strong-arming Israel into actually working to make peace. But that effort is going to need to start in the West Bank and start working through with the P.A. a long-term solution to the refugee issue. Hamas needs to either accept the two-state concept at least in principle, or the Palestinians need to kick their butts out of power in Gaza. Neither of those scenarios look even remotely likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":".  Fixed rather essential spelling mistake which sort of changed the meaning of a whole sentence. Whoops. My bad. 08-09-2014, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T04:54:26-07:00","id":220931,"title":"","content":"Australian Jew here, maybe I can provide a perspective, not being from Israel or the States?<br /> <br /> Now, I think we can agree that both sides have done some pretty dicey things, for some pretty dicey reasons. And we can also agree that the situation is <u>immensely</u> complex historically, politically, economically, socially and theologically. However, all that said:<br /> <br /> While Israel may have done some pretty dicey things (maybe necessary or understandable, but questionable), the national identity of the countries needs to be considered in any opinion on the matter, I think. Let's take Israel for a moment: created as a country so a people, who had historically suffered horrific injustices for literally centuries, from pretty much every major country in the world (the US included), consisting of (but not limited to) being forced to live in slums, being denied access to basic services or forcibly expelled, and <i>outright mass murder </i>(which pretty much nobody blinked an eye at), had somewhere to go, and not only not face being beaten and killed,but actually be accepted. This is, I think, an important point that people tend to gloss over: the Jewish people have not had a country of their own, or a place they could go, pretty much ever, and the establishment of Israel promised an end to this, and in fact represented the fulfilment of some pretty seriously important prophecies. It's roughly equivalent (not exactly, but illustrative) to Jesus coming down to the Western world, and saying &quot;'Sup? Screw this mortal coil, come hang out in Heaven where you don't need to worry about death or pain <i>ever again</i>.&quot; And they get their country, and set it up, and then find themselves in a fight for their very existence by a group who want to take that from them? Is it really all that surprising that they may have over-reacted, and are not willing to compromise? And when American people say things like &quot;<i>they wouldn't have a country if it wasn't for us</i>&quot;, it doesn't just come off as being yet more American arrogance and entitlement like it does to the rest of the world, it's particularly raw because the American government, on multiple occasions, actively tried to kick out or oppress the Jewish people, and pretty much stood back and did nothing while the Germans conducted one of the more successful and blatant genocide attempts. So, the idea of the Americans giving the Jewish people Israel comes off as pretty bad, because they see it as something they freaking <i>earned</i>, and the US being far from the most innocent of their historical tormentors. Now, you might say that a lot of that was a long time ago, and you'd be right, but it's still very much a major part of how Israel sees itself, and the Jewish people more generally. So, when they're being &quot;disrespectful&quot;, maybe think about where that's coming from, and think maybe the US has some disrespect coming.<br /> <br /> Now, let's examine Palestine, shall we? Now, granted, this is a country I know less about historically, but I do know that they are kind of similar to the Jews in that they've never really, properly had a country of their own. Not because they didn't have one, but because they kept being invaded and dominated by their various neighbours. Even now, a lot of countries (including the US) refuses to acknowledge the state of Palestine as a country in its own right. And all of a sudden, they have a pretty sizable chunk taken out of their land by the UN (who I believe they still don't get a casting vote with? Not certain about that) and given to a people they have not historically gotten along well with, and told that they, basically, have to suck it. Now, like Israel, they've done some pretty dicey stuff in the past and present, and they're kind of fragmented these days culturally still. However, a lot of the issues are that they have been shown, again and again throughout history, that if they want something (like, say, a place to live and call their own), they have to fight, and fight dirty: god knows their enemies will, and if they aren't every bit as ruthless, they'll lose. Again.<br /> <br /> So, essentially, saying one side or the other is 'to blame' for this situation is oversimplifying the situation, in my view. It's entirely too complex, and while I have no idea how a peaceful situation could be arranged, assuming one is even possible at this stage (even if one side <i>did</i> commit, genuinely, to peace, the other side would think of it as a trap and attack, or remember all the times in the past when they did exactly the same thing to the now-aggressors), I do know that pointing fingers is not going to be productive. They've both suffered horrendously, they've both done terrible things, the situation has been exploited, and in some cases encouraged, by a lot of other countries. So any peace cannot begin with the idea of one side being more or less to blame, or even all the blame resting on those two states or groups. Any country that wants to make peace has to own up to their part in it, and try to approach the situation in good faith, and with respect to the experiences of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T05:44:31-07:00","id":220963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220931#post220931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When American people say things like, &quot;They wouldn't have a country if it wasn't for us,&quot; [snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever heard an American say that, though? I haven't. Hell, I'm pretty sure most Americans have no idea we helped found Israel, or that it was founded within living memory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T05:55:09-07:00","id":220965,"title":"","content":"I get tired of hearing that Israel should get a free pass targeting children because of events that happened 70 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T06:05:08-07:00","id":220970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220965#post220965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get tired of hearing that Israel should get a free pass targeting children because of events that happened 70 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying Allan53 said that, or are you just making a general observation about your personal tastes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T06:17:17-07:00","id":220975,"title":"","content":"General observation....<a href=\"http://www.alternet.org/israels-brutal-war-palestinian-children\" target=\"_blank\">Israel\u2019s Brutal War on Palestinian Children</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T07:01:36-07:00","id":220986,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220963#post220963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever heard an American say that, though? I haven't. Hell, I'm pretty sure most Americans have no idea we helped found Israel, or that it was founded within living memory.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=217143#post217143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my opinion, the biggest issue at work here has nothing whatsoever to do with the Palestinians, but rather the internal politics of both the United States and Israel. The U.S. could probably force an end to this whole nightmare if we could muster the political willpower to use our economic and political influence. Gaza is a chaotic nightmare, but the settlement issue in the West Bank is more clear-cut (against Israel), and ultimately easier to resolve. There is <i>absolutely</i> no legal justification for those settlements, and they're causing all sorts of international headaches for us (because of our support of Israel). What burns me is that jerks like Netanyahu <i><u>wouldn't have a country </u></i><u>if it wasn't for us</u>, but anytime we start pushing them on the issue, they show us nothing but a really disgusting level of disrespect (the Kinesset's statements regarding V.P. Kerry lately are a good example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Added the underline in the above for clarity's sake, and left the surrounding paragraphs to give it some context. Now, I'm not saying expressing this is <i>common</i>, I don't talk to enough Americans to speculate about that. But I have come across it occasionally, and it is in line with the general arrogance the US is perceived as having.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220965#post220965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get tired of hearing that Israel should get a free pass targeting children because of events that happened 70 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220970#post220970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying Allan53 said that, or are you just making a general observation about your personal tastes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did try to be clear that all involved parties had done bad things, in some cases going back centuries, and that the context did not make those things not bad. Did that not come across? Because I don't think I could have emphasised it too much more. What it does do is affect how the situation needs to be approached.<br /> <br /> And it's not 'because of events that happened 70 years ago'. It's (by that I mean what I'm getting at) is the systematic, sustained and accepted pattern of prejudice and<i> repeated attempted genocide</i>, by many, many countries, including the US, going back literally centuries. The Nazi holocaust was a terrible, terrible thing, and it's very, very relevant to Israel, but it was really just the latest, and arguably one of the more 'successful', example of stuff that had been happening for centuries. But that pattern preceding it did not suddenly cease to be relevant just because of that terrible situation: they still happened, and they're still very much a part of the Israeli national identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T06:07:14-07:00","id":222030,"title":"","content":"My one and only contribution to this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2frJ3e0hxPE\" data-code=\"2frJ3e0hxPE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2frJ3e0hxPE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> - Azrael &quot;Knives&quot; Firestorm, Malkavian Reeve of the New Mexico Anarch territory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T01:33:49-07:00","id":222973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220963#post220963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever heard an American say that, though? I haven't. Hell, I'm pretty sure most Americans have no idea we helped found Israel, or that it was founded within living memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I am an American and I am saying that. I am also going on record at this time as standing by that statement 100%.<br /> <br /> The Israelis <i>would not have a freaking country </i>if not for the United States of America.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220931#post220931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And when American people say things like &quot;<i>they wouldn't have a country if it wasn't for us</i>&quot;, it doesn't just come off as being yet more American arrogance and entitlement like it does to the rest of the world, it's particularly raw because the American government, on multiple occasions, actively tried to kick out or oppress the Jewish people, and pretty much stood back and did nothing while the Germans conducted one of the more successful and blatant genocide attempts...</div> </div> </div> </div>And lost 400,000 people while doing that whole lot of nothing, apparently.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/188860-general-politics-thread?p=220931#post220931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, the idea of the Americans giving the Jewish people Israel comes off as pretty bad, because they see it as something they freaking <i>earned</i>, and the US being far from the most innocent of their historical tormentors. Now, you might say that a lot of that was a long time ago, and you'd be right, but it's still very much a major part of how Israel sees itself, and the Jewish people more generally. So, when they're being &quot;disrespectful&quot;, maybe think about where that's coming from, and think maybe the US has some disrespect coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that the Israelis didn't earn it. I said that they wouldn't have a country if not for us.<br /> <br /> First off, if not for the rapid introduction of forty F-4 Phantom fighters and three dozen A-4 Skyhawk attack aircraft in the 1973 fracas, they would almost certainly have lost the air war, and very likely the ground war upon losing air superiority. Those aircraft were U.S.A.F. aircraft that were thrown into the fight (rapidly repainted) in a matter of days. These were not simply to replace the devastating loses that the IAF sustained, but also had up-to-date ECM gear not found on their Israeli counterparts. This finally allowed the IAF to counter the &quot;new&quot; SA-6 threat that totally took the IAF by surprise.<br /> <br /> Historically, Israel has spent around 10% of GDP annually upon military expenditures. In the 1980s, this ballooned to about 25%. For reference, Iran spends about 7%. The only country that spends about that much (that I could find on a cursory search) was North Korea -- at 10%. That is simply not sustainable. Iran is practically bankrupt. Why? Because it doesn't have the United States pumping three and a quarter <i>billion dollars </i>annually into it's military coffers (never mind the <i>minor</i> issue of it's disco-era equipment). At current spending levels, Israel is seeing roughly 20% of it's military budget financed <i>entirely</i> by American taxpayers. This includes roughly 80% of their Iron Dome system, and <i>practically all </i>of their precision guided munitions currently being expended to bounce rubble in Gaza (and just watch, in the next few months, Israel is going to quietly come begging for the U.S. Congress to replenish their nearly-dry stocks of smart-bombs -- this is a pattern).<br /> <br /> The other reason why Israel doesn't look like Iran is that they aren't under international sanctions (because remember, permanently displacing civilians is actually illegal under international law when you are a declared &quot;occupying power&quot;). That's also due to the United States. We've been running interference for them at the U.N. for decades. Netanyahu is entirely comfortable doing what-the-heck-ever he wants, because he knows that there isn't squat anyone can do about it at the U.N. so long as the big-brother with the veto is standing behind him.<br /> <br /> So yes, the United States has done some cr**py things, and yes we probably do deserve some disrespect coming our way... But sure as heck<i> NOT </i>from Netanyahu nor the rest of that bunch...<br /> <br /> ...because <i>they wouldn't have a freaking country if not for us</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-09-2014, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:16:18-07:00","id":223237,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the US armed Israel and they're given some of the best weapons. The US even looked the other way when Israel was developing nuclear weapons. The US stood by and didn't do anything when their own USS Liberty was deliberately attacked and 34 Americans were killed. And they get billions in military aid every year. Considering how many people Israel kills in retaliation for the loss of one soldier, it's no wonder that it's leaders have had a sneering contempt for the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:25:34-07:00","id":223495,"title":"","content":"...And yet, I'm not being (terribly) critical of Israel's current activity in Gaza. Hamas instigated the whole thing -- and purely for its own selfish and, frankly, revolting purposes. They have no hope of defending their own civilians, so they pick a fight with Israel and essentially daring them to hit back. Then make demands that they have absolutely no leverage to force upon Israel -- thus ensuring that they can keep the whole thing going and continue to score brownie-points with the rest of the extremist crowd in the Middle East. The whole Hamas thing is so cynical. And yes, they <i>are</i> trying to get the Israelis to cause civilian casualties -- there's now news organizations that have footage of Hamas firing rockets from the courtyard of a hotel.<br /> <br /> The point I think gets lost is that the thing in Gaza is a complete sideshow, and is distracting from the real issues at play here -- issues that Israel is happily ignoring because they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-09-2014, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:46:16-07:00","id":223710,"title":"","content":"Hamas didn't start this latest round.<br /> Israeli officials knew all along that Hamas was not behind the kidnapping which was the pretext for the latest round of fighting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://nymag.com/daily/intelligencer/2014/07/hamas-didnt-kidnap-the-israeli-teens-after-all.html\" target=\"_blank\">It Turns Out Hamas Didn\u2019t Kidnap and Kill the 3 Israeli Teens After All</a><br /> <br /> Israel hasn't anything to gain by peace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T19:23:19-07:00","id":223788,"title":"","content":"Okay, first off, nobody knows who did the kidnapping thing. But it's irrelevant anyway. When I say Hamas instigated the whole thing, I'm referencing the attack-tunnels. That's the real reason Israel went in. The kidnapping was simply a pretext (regardless of who was actually responsible -- which may still have been Hamas for all anyone knows). After losing their last allies in Egypt, Hamas was spoiling for something that would divert attention away from the reality that refusing Israeli demands to disarm was a hopeless course as far as their civilians were concerned. The Israelis were looking for an excuse to &quot;mow the grass&quot;. It was essentially a political stunt for both sides, but if Hamas hadn't been preparing those tunnels, Israel probably wouldn't have gone in.<br /> <br /> And when this thing finally dies out (which it will), it will have allowed Israel to divert attention away from the West Bank settlements, and the refugee issue, and for Hamas to divert attention away from the futility of their strategy of refusal of the two-state solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T14:42:36-07:00","id":224493,"title":"","content":"Disappear for a few days and man this goes places. Interesting places too...<br /> <br /> Glad to see that level heads prevailed, again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"20